==========================================================================
A single vertex-vertex coincidence, and how each measure counts it
==========================================================================
coincidences (v,j)      : [(0, 0)]
crossPairs              : 0 []
segDeg  entries         : 2 [(0, 0), (6, 0)]
segDegP entries         : 2 [(0, 0), (6, 0)]
degPts (POINTS, ncard)  : 1 [(0, 0)]

the ONE coincidence point is counted
   segDeg + segDegP : 4 times
   degPts           : 1 time(s)

M_seg = |crossPairs| + |segDeg| + |segDegP| = 4
M_pt  = |crossPairs| + |degPts|             = 1

VERDICT: M_seg overcounts this coincidence by 3 units.
         Clearing it must be paid for 4 crossings under M_seg, but only 1 under M_pt.

==========================================================================
CONTROL -- on a 9.2-style degeneracy (vertex strictly INSIDE a side)
the two measures agree, which is why M_seg works there
==========================================================================
coincidences            : []  (empty)
Q[0] strictly inside P-side 0 : True
segDeg + segDegP        : 1
degPts                  : 1
overcount               : 0  <- ZERO, the two measures agree

==========================================================================
SANITY -- the primitives are not permissive
==========================================================================
on_segment rejects an off-line point  : True
on_segment accepts an endpoint        : True
proper_cross on a clean crossing      : True
proper_cross rejects a touch          : True
